# ==============================================================================
# .htpasswd.example — Nginx HTTP Basic Authentication Template
# ==============================================================================
# DO NOT ADD REAL CREDENTIALS OR REAL PASSWORD HASHES TO THIS TEMPLATE.
# DO NOT COMMIT THE ACTUAL .htpasswd FILE TO VERSION CONTROL.
#
# Production .htpasswd file must be generated directly on the EC2 production host
# at path: docker/nginx/.htpasswd
#
# Generate a secure bcrypt-hashed (.htpasswd) file on the host using Docker:
#
#   docker run --rm httpd:alpine htpasswd -B -c -b /dev/stdout <username> <password> > docker/nginx/.htpasswd
#   chmod 600 docker/nginx/.htpasswd
#
# Format:
# <username>:<bcrypt-or-apr1-hashed-password>
#
# Example (placeholder only - NOT a real credential):
# soc_analyst:$2y$10$EXAMPLE_HASH_DO_NOT_USE_PLACEHOLDER_ONLY_REPLACE_ON_HOST
